  "sources": [
    {"title": "Neuron xS30 Modbus map (neuron_xs30_modbus_map.xlsx)", "url": "https://kb.unipi.technology/_media/files:products:extensions_gateyways:extensions:modbus_maps/neuron_xs30_modbus_map.xlsx", "note": "Sheets Registers - group 1, Coils - group 1 and Description; listed on https://kb.unipi.technology/en:hw:04-extensions:downloads"}
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The spreadsheet is titled Neuron xS30: the xS modules are the extensions of the Unipi Neuron controllers. Unipi also publishes per-model holding-register maps for the xS series (xS11, xS51-xS54), which are separate files.",
    "Addresses are those of the column 'Via Unit 1' (the module addressed directly, group 1). The column 'Via Unit 0' gives the same address for the shared registers but has no entries for the RS485 configuration registers (500-504), which are included here.",
    "Connection defaults (baud rate, parity, unit id) are not stated in the spreadsheet; the module's Modbus address is configurable (1-254) in the register named Modbus Address Configuration.",
    "Registers marked reserved, internal or obsolete in the spreadsheet are left out. Multi-register values are big-endian (most significant register first), as the Description sheet states.",
    "Coils repeat the digital inputs, outputs and some settings that also appear as bits of holding registers."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
